File What is in it <code>src/core/main.ts</code> arguments and the commands. Usage is written at its top <code>src/core/apihandlers/eli.ts</code> the API: its address, shapes of answers, addresses of every part of an act <code>src/core/resources/store.ts</code> where gathered things are written, and how (<code>.part</code>, then rename) <code>src/core/crawl.ts</code> one polite walk over addresses of an API: own name, pace, queue in memory <code>src/core/methods/gather.ts</code> index → lists → years, then files of acts year by year; <code>--since</code> for changes <code>src/core/methods/seal.ts</code> checksums of gathered files: writing records, checking files against them <code>src/core/methods/compile.ts</code> tables of details and references from raw files <code>src/core/parsing/text.ts</code> markdown from HTML, with records that tie both <code>src/core/apihandlers/sejm.ts</code> another source: processes and prints of Sejm <code>src/core/apihandlers/saos.ts</code> another source: court judgments <code>src/core/methods/checkup.ts</code> the browser visiting websites, with Crawlee <code>PlaywrightCrawler</code> and Camoufox <code>src/core/resources/hub.ts</code> comparison and sync with Hugging Face, with <code>@huggingface/hub</code> <p>Four rules keep it readable:</p> <ul> <li>Addresses and data stay out of handlers. A handler in <code>gather.ts</code> says   what happens; where to ask is in <code>eli.ts</code> and where to write is in   <code>store.ts</code>.</li> <li>One command, one file. <code>main.ts</code> only reads arguments and calls.</li> <li>No flat scope. Files sit in the directory of their kind under   <code>src/core/</code>: <code>apihandlers/</code> for sources, <code>methods/</code> for what commands do,   <code>parsing/</code> for raw files into text, <code>resources/</code> for the local sides and   Hugging Face. A new kind gets a new directory.</li> <li>Types and interfaces live in <code>src/core/vars/</code>. One per file,   <code>types/&lt;Name&gt;.type.ts</code> or <code>interfaces/&lt;Name&gt;.interface.ts</code>, with a default   export and no directories inside. The <code>index.ts</code> of each directory puts   them into namespaces, <code>GatheringScope</code> and <code>HuggingfaceScope</code>, and code   takes them from there:</li> </ul> <pre><code>import type { GatheringScope } from "../vars/interfaces/index.js";
import type { GatheringScope as GatheringTypes } from "../vars/types/index.js";

function trusted(act: GatheringScope.Act, part: GatheringTypes.Part) {}
</code></pre> <p><code>src/cli-command.js</code>, <code>src/cli-repl.js</code>, <code>src/desktopapp/</code>, <code>src/webgui/</code> and <code>src/webserver/</code> are beginnings of other ways into the same core. They are not wired to anything yet.</p>
